Parquet writer: dictionary policy, dictionary page size and column encodings.

GlamDB lets a collection choose Parquet dictionary use and explicit value
encodings per column. The pinned ParquetWriter exposes neither. This patch
reads, in Open() before the output file is created:

  write.parquet.dict-enabled                     file default, true|false
  write.parquet.dict-enabled.column.<field-name> column override
  write.parquet.dict-size-bytes                  dictionary page limit (Iceberg's name)
  write.parquet.encoding.column.<field-name>     plain, delta_binary_packed,
                                                 delta_length_byte_array,
                                                 delta_byte_array,
                                                 byte_stream_split, rle

Encodings are checked against the column's physical type. Arrow ignores an
explicit encoding while the column's dictionary is enabled and always falls
back to PLAIN on dictionary overflow, so an explicit encoding requires the
column's dictionary to be disabled; enabling a dictionary for a boolean column
(which Arrow never dictionary-encodes) is rejected instead of ignored.
Plain is supported for decimal at every precision (INT32, INT64 or fixed
bytes); other decimal encodings are not exposed by GlamDB's type-level policy.

Applies after 0002-parquet-column-compression.patch. Pinned revision:
apache/iceberg-cpp 64dc66f159bd62c9817a96d74cbce767268934d0 (v0.4.0); upstream
main 36e0d1a has no such properties.

